 - **Fields** (getters that read data, never stored numbers): `expected`, `module`, `session` (`session ?? session_id`), `priority` (latest `{priority:{score,why,by}}` line or `null`), `commits` (short hashes from `{"commit":"…"}` lines, no duplicates; `commit(hash)` appends one). Replay reads both lines without leaving the legacy mapping. `sessions` ([{id, task}], node appends it), `source` (voice-app | vscode | dictate | servex:<id>; an old `/` doc path reads as `doc`) and `cost` (USD, computed from the agents on this task via `Task.cost_resolver`, wired in `Servex/agents/Agents.js`).
 - **`completion_score()`** (0 to 1, the one number; `completion` is its alias; 2026-11-04): score = 1 if `checked_by`; else the mean of the scores of its parts (subtasks not stopped, child sessions, counted owner prompts, to any depth); a plain task with no parts is 1 if complete else 0, but a **session** with nothing to score is `null` ("needs review": no tasks means the work was never recorded, not that it was done). A parent's mean counts a child session that has nothing to score of its own as 1 if complete and 0 if not (`part_score`), so a session whose child sessions carry the work keeps its number; `Task.mean` itself leaves nulls out, and all-null is null; `Task.show(score)` is the one place that turns a score into "62%" or "needs review", so every caller handles null through it. `tally()` counts created/finished/stopped/open, `unscored` (sessions that read null) and `proof_problem` finishes. Printed for any session by `node Server/session-query.mjs --report <id>`; why this formula and not finished/created: [Session readme](../Session/readme.md#the-one-formula). Test: `node completion.test.mjs`.
-- **No silent endings** (`closeout_line(at)`, `open_items()`, `Task.is_closeout`): when a session or task is closed under a score of 1, one task waiting on the owner (`{"wait":{"on":"owner","what":…}}`, id `open-items`, then `open-items-2`) is filed that lists the open items by id, title and state. The rule is `Task#closeout_line`; `Servex/OpenItems.js` calls it after any closing line (stop, complete, finish, unclosed, closed_by, landed_at) reaches a record, from the two append chokepoints (`page_tools.js write_line`, `TaskLoop.js write_line`). It compares the replay before and after the line, so a repeat or replayed close files nothing, and it files nothing when there is nothing open to list. Closeout tasks are left out of the score, `reopened()` and the `complete()` open-child check, so the waiting task never reopens the record it was filed on. `list_waiting` (`Servex/cards/Cards.js`) lists owner-waiting tasks from `ai/index.json` next to card needs. Known gaps (writes that bypass both chokepoints and file nothing): `Server/PromptRecords.mjs`, `Server/CloseoutWalk.mjs --apply`, and `RecordWriter.append_once` (append.mjs and StaleClose when Servex is down). Tests: `node Servex/OpenItems.test.mjs`. PROPOSED, off by default: it files only with SERVEX_OPEN_ITEMS=on; dry run: node Servex/OpenItems.mjs --dry-run (doc/completion.md).
